From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] accuracy defaults, and all 240 lines

bsnes is shipped here for its accuracy, and its libretro defaults trade
it for speed. The defaults are now the accurate paths: the cycle-based
PPU instead of the scanline renderer, the exact DSP, coprocessors in
lockstep, and the real coprocessor programs where the firmware is
present (HLE stays the fallback without it).

No overscan crop. bsnes draws a 224-line game on lines 8-231 of its
240, so the picture is the same with or without the default crop of 8,
but a game in the 239-line mode loses its edges to it, and the frame
size stops changing when a game switches mode. The aspect ratio follows
the lines shown: 8:7 pixels over 240 lines is 128/105.

--- a/bsnes/target-libretro/libretro_core_options.h
+++ b/bsnes/target-libretro/libretro_core_options.h
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@ struct retro_core_option_v2_definition option_defs_us[] = {
          { "16", "16 Lines" },
          { NULL, NULL },
       },
-      "8"
+      "0"
    },
    {
       "bsnes_blur_emulation",
@@ -246,7 +246,7 @@ struct retro_core_option_v2_definition option_defs_us[] = {
          { "OFF", "disabled" },
          { NULL, NULL },
       },
-      "ON"
+      "OFF"
    },
